id: PREFER:7000006
name: unit of optical density
is_a: PREFER:9000004 ! unit

[Term]
id: PREFER:7000007
name: dimensionless unit
is_a: PREFER:9000004 ! unit

[Term]
id: PREFER:7000008
name: revolution per minute
is_a: PREFER:9000004 ! unit

[Term]
id: PREFER:9000000
name: precision fermentation process control variable
def: "An information content entity that represents a parameter or setting about a system, which is realized as input or configuration in controlling or regulating a fermentation process, thereby affecting the behavior, operation, or outcome of that process." []
comment: A decision was made to classify this as a information content entity rather than realizable entity (a realizable entity that inheres in a system and is realized in processes of controlling or regulating a process, serving as a parameter or setting that affects or determines the behavior, operation, or outcome of that process) as the intention was to emphasize the informational role rather than physical realisation of the control.
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
property_value: dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596" xsd:string

[Term]
id: PREFER:9000001
name: precision fermentation process measurement variable
def: "An information content entity about a precision fermentation process that specifically represents measurable attributes or values that are the outcomes of a measurement process aimed at determining characteristics of said process." []
synonym: "PREcision FERmentation process measurement variable" EXACT []
synonym: "process measurement variable" BROAD []
xref: VO:0010241
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
property_value: dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596" xsd:string

[Term]
id: PREFER:9000002
name: precision fermentation process calculated variable
def: "An information content entity about a process that is the output of a calculation or computation based on one or more measured or other input variables, representing derived or computed attributes related to the fermentation process." []
synonym: "process calculated variable" EXACT []
synonym: "process computed variable" EXACT []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
property_value: dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596" xsd:string

[Term]
id: PREFER:9000003
name: precision fermentation process
def: "A process that involves precision fermentation." []
comment: Precision fermentation is a biotechnological method used in industrial or research settings that employs genetically engineered or adaptatively laboratory-evolved (ALE) microorganisms (such as bacteria, yeast, fungi or microalgae) to produce specific, high-value compounds with precise molecular structures. This process involves controlled environments—such as operating bioreactor parameters(e.g., temperature, pH, dissolved oxygen, agitation, nutrient feed) and upstream preparation conditions(e.g., pre-culture growth, strain storage, and defined media composition)—where microbial metabolism is optimized to synthesize target products, such as proteins, enzymes, or bioactive molecules, often with greater efficiency, yield, and specificity than traditional fermentation methods.
is_a: BFO:0000015 ! process
relationship: BAO_0002009 GO:0006113 ! fermentation

[Term]
id: PREFER:9000004
name: unit
def: "An information content entity that represents a standard quantity or measurement used to express the magnitude of a quantity." []
comment: The decision to utilise https://units-of-measurement.org/ meant that we did not want to commit to any unit ontologies. We hence created our own parent class to parent units. Interoperability of units can be achieved by the matches in units-of-measurement, and this term should only be used to constraining in modelling.
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

